'''{{PAGENAME}}''' are neutral [[creatures]] commonly found in [[Grassland|grasslands]]. They are a source of [[Raw Wild Mutton|meat]], [[Fresh Mouflon Hide|hide]], and most notably, [[Wool]]. Individual mouflon can be domesticated into [[Sheep]] through [[Taming]].

==Acquisition==
Mouflon spawn individually as entities in most [[grassland]] [[terrain]] at all times of year.

Dispatched mouflon can be skinned, cleaned, and butchered via right click by [[Hearthling|Hearthlings]] that have learned [[Hunting]]. While mouflon corpses cannot be placed in a Hearthling's [[inventory]], they can be lifted and stored within objects such as [[Cart|Carts]] and [[Shed|Sheds]].

The [[quality]] of a dispatched mouflon is calculated upon death, and its total is hardcapped by both a Hearthling's [[Survival]] and the quality of any [[Weapons|weapon]] or [[Sharp Tool|sharp tool]] used to kill them.

== Behavior ==
Mouflon are neutral until attacked, at which point they will initiate [[combat]] and give chase. Mouflon run at above Hearthling run speed, so a Hearthling must be sprinting, riding a vehicle, or on [[Horse|horseback]] to outrun or give chase.

=== Domestication ===
Mouflon may, over time, be domesticated by any Hearthling that has learned [[Taming]] once successfully fed a [[Clover]] and [[Rope|leashed]] to a [[Hitching Post]]. After multiple rounds of "breaking in" via combat, the taming process will be complete and the mouflon will, with a puff of pink smoke, immediately transform into a sheep.

A mouflon has no gender, and as such whether it transforms into a ram or ewe is determined at random upon transformation. This means that a particularly unlucky Hearthling may end up with a small herd of only ewes, or vice versa, before obtaining a breeding pair. For this reason, simultaneous domestication of multiple mouflon is advised.

=== Combat ===
Mouflon are about as strong as a [[badger]], with the exception of a higher [[Agility]] stat equivalent to 45-50. They throw out Mule Kicks and Low Horn Swipes quickly, and will often spam Swift Evasion to remove their own openings. Unless a Hearthling possesses similar Agility, or has high enough [[Unarmed Combat|Unarmed]] and [[Melee Combat]] to deal ample openings to force them into a defensive state, using a [[Stone Axe|Stone]] or [[Tinker's Throwing Axe]] to deliver a mighty Cleave or Full Circle while the mouflon's {{RoB color|oppressive|Cornered}} opening is high should encourage it to flee, at which point it can be chased and defeated while running.

When Taming a mouflon, Hearthlings should wear good armor and expect it to sustain durability damage. Quick Barrage or Sideswipe is recommended, so long as the mouflon's {{RoB color|sweeping|Reeling}} opening isn't high enough to inflict grievously high damage. If a Hearthling cannot ignore their own openings, enlisting allies to assist in the Taming process is advised.

